  "question": {
    "text": "A nucleus with mass number <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>220</mn></math> initially at rest emits an <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>α</mi></math>-particle. If the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi></math> value of the reaction is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5.5</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>MeV</mi></math>, then calculate the kinetic energy of the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>α</mi></math>-particle."
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>4.4</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>MeV</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>5.4</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>MeV</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>5.6</mn><mo>&#xA0;</mo><mi>MeV</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>6.5</mn><mo>&#xA0;</mo><mi>MeV</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Given that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mtext>5.5</mtext><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>MeV</mi></math> ... (i)<br /><br />From conservation of linear momentum,<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math><br /><br /><math><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo maxsize=\"1.00em\">(</mo><mn>216</mn><mi>m</mi><mo maxsize=\"1.00em\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mo maxsize=\"1.00em\">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>m</mi><mo maxsize=\"1.00em\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></math>&nbsp; &nbsp; (As <math><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>K</mi><mi>m</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow></math>)<br /><br />&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>54</mn><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> ... (ii)<br /><br />Solving Eqs. (i) and (ii), we get<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo></math>K.E. of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>α</mi></math>-particle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext>5.4</mtext><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>MeV</mi></math>."
  }
